Z||000000||Alex2004||04-29-2001||03:15 PM||||My radiator fan has never came on, not even w/ the a/c on.  Some of the members here told me it was a relay or it could be the fan motor it's self.  well today i took the relay off but how do i test it to see if it's a relay or not.  There are 6 wires on the plug, Red, green w/ wht, lt green w/ blk, gray, and 2 big black wires.  which of these do i "hot wire" or whatever it's called to see if it's the relay or fan?  LMK,  thanks! oh, it's an 84 SE<P>Alex....    <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 04-29-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Alex2004||04-29-2001||09:00 PM||||Thanks for all your replies!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But i found the problem!  It was a really bad ground, so i fixed that and it still wouldn't come on so i took the relay out and ran a wire from the hot wire over to the last black wire and it worked!  So all i need is a relay!  Thanks!<P>Alex...||||reg||10
